    <!-- DACS 2.7 -->
    <bioghist>
      <head>Historical Note</head>
      <p>Jeff Peterson was a longtime and distinguished chair of the Mary Riley Styles Library Board
        of Trustees, and Village Preservation and Improvement Society from 2007-2015. The primary
        responsibility of the Library Board of Trustees is general oversight of the Mary Riley
        Styles Public Library establishing policies and necessary rules for library management. The
        Board makes recommendations to the library director regarding budget preparation and advises
        the City Council and mayor. </p>
      <p>Mr. Peterson's contribution to the development of the Mary Riley Styles Public Library is
        invaluable. </p>
    </bioghist>
    <!-- DACS 3.1 -->
    <scopecontent>
      <head>Scope and Content</head>
      <p>The materials include Projects, Plans, Reports, Surveys, Memorandums, and Notes.</p>
      <p>The archive is organized as follows: <list>
          <item>Series 1: Library Board of Trustees </item>
          <item>Series 2: Planning Commission</item>
          <item>Series 3: Preliminary Research</item>
          <item>Series 4: Development </item>
          <item>Series 5: Memorandums</item>
          <item>Series 6: Reports</item>
        </list></p>
    </scopecontent>
    <!-- DACS 3.2 -->
    <arrangement>
      <head>Arrangement</head>
      <p>Most documents were originally organized by subject or chronologically. The archivist
        organized the documents into a series in chronological order.</p>
    </arrangement>
